{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jas-2-1","title":"James 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 It is not agreeable to Christian profession to regard the rich, and to despise the poor brethren; 13 rather we are to be loving and merciful; 14 and not to boast of faith where no deeds are; 17 which is but a dead faith; 19 the faith of the devils; 21 not of Abraham; 25 nor Rahab.</p>\n<p>the faith. Ac 20:21; 24:24; Col 1:4; 1Ti 1:19; Tit 1:1; 2Pe 1:1; Re 14:12 the Lord. Ps 24:7-10; 1Co 2:8; Tit 2:13; Heb 1:3 with. 3,9; 3:17; Le 19:15; De 1:17; 16:19; 2Ch 19:7; Pr 24:23; 28:21 Mt 22:16; Ro 1:11; 1Ti 5:21; Jude 1:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-2","title":"James 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>assembly. Gr. synagogue. gold. Es 3:10; 8:2; Lu 15:22 goodly. Ge 27:15; Mt 11:8,9 in vile. Isa 64:6; Zec 3:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-3","title":"James 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>ye. Jude 1:16 in a good place. or well, or, seemly. to the. 6; Isa 65:5; Lu 7:44-46; 2Co 8:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-4","title":"James 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>partial. 1:1-27; Job 34:19; Mal 2:9 judges. 4:11; Job 21:27; Ps 58:1; 82:2; 109:31; Mt 7:1-5; Joh 7:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-5","title":"James 2:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Hearken. Jud 9:7; 1Ki 22:28; Job 34:10; 38:14; Pr 7:24; 8:32; Mr 7:14; Ac 7:2 Hath not. 1:9; Isa 14:32; 29:19; Zep 3:12; Zec 11:7,11; Mt 11:5; Lu 6:20 Lu 9:57,58; 16:22,25; Joh 7:48; 1Co 1:26-28; 2Co 8:9 rich. Pr 8:17-21; Lu 12:21; 1Co 3:21-23; 2Co 4:15; 6:10; Eph