 all the precepts of the law has broken the yoke, dissolved the covenant, and exposed the law to contempt; and so has he done who has only broken one precept;\" they also taught, \"that he who observed any principal command was equal to him who kept the whole law,\" and gave for an example the forsaking of idolatry. To correct this false doctrine was the object James had in view.</p>\n<p>whosoever. De 27:26; Mt 5:18,19; Ga 3:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-11","title":"James 2:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>he said that. or, that law, which said. Do not commit. Ex 20:13,14; De 5:17,18; Mt 5:21-28; 19:18; Mr 10:19; Lu 18:20 Ro 13:9 Now. Le 4:2,13,22; Ps 130:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-12","title":"James 2:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>speak. Php 4:8; Col 3:17; 2Pe 1:4-8 the. 8; 1:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-13","title":"James 2:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>he. 5:4; Ge 42:21; Jud 1:7; Job 22:6-10; Pr 21:13; Isa 27:11; Mt 5:7 Mt 6:15; 7:1,2; 18:28-35; 25:41-46; Lu 16:25 and. Ps 85:10; Jer 9:24; Eze 33:11; Mic 7:18; Eph 1:6,7; 2:4-7 1Jo 4:8-16,18,19 rejoiceth. or, glorieth.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-14","title":"James 2:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>What. 16; Jer 7:8; Ro 2:25; 1Co 13:3; 1Ti 4:8; Heb 13:9 though. 18,26; 1:22-25; Mt 5:20; 7:21-23,26,27; Lu 6:49; Ac 8:13,21; 15:9 1Co 13:2; 16:22; Ga 5:6,13; 1Th 1:3; 1Ti 1:5; Tit 1:16; 3:8 Heb 11:7,8,17; 2Pe 1:5; 1Jo 5:4,5 can. 1Co 15:2; Eph 2:8-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jas-2-15","title":"James 2:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JAS","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":2,"ve